5.	Class Diagram and/or Sequence Diagrams (15 points)
The system follows a modular service-oriented architecture with clearly defined entities and service layers.
Core Entities
•	User 
•	StockSymbol 
•	Candle (OHLCV data) 
•	IndicatorResult 
•	BacktestRun 
•	BacktestResult 
•	Watchlist 
•	WatchlistItem 
Service Components
AuthService:
•	register_user 
•	authenticate 
StockService:
•	ingest_price_data 
•	get_price_series 
IndicatorService:
•	compute_sma 
•	compute_rsi 
•	compute_ema 
•	compute_bollinger_bands 
•	compute_macd 
BacktestService:
•	run_sma_threshold_backtest 
•	run_sma_crossover_backtest 
•	run_rsi_threshold_backtest 
•	run_macd_crossover_backtest 
•	run_bollinger_breakout_backtest 
NewsService:
•	fetch_news_from_rss 
These services interact through REST API endpoints and operate on shared database entities.
6.	Operating Environment (5 points)
•  Operating Systems: macOS, Linux, Windows 
•  Backend Runtime: Python 3.10+ 
•  Framework: FastAPI 
•  Frontend: React (Vite) 
•  Database: SQLite (development), PostgreSQL (production) 
•  Network: Internet access required for external data sources 
•  Port: Backend runs on port 8000, frontend on port 5173
7.	Assumptions and Dependencies (5 points)
Assumptions
•	The system operates in a single-node environment for development. 
•	End-of-day market data is sufficient for analysis. 
•	Users interact through a web browser interface. 
•	External APIs return consistent and valid data. 
Dependencies
•	Yahoo Finance API for historical market data 
•	Google News RSS for news integration 
•	FastAPI and Python ecosystem 
•	SQLite / PostgreSQL database systems 
•	JWT libraries for authentication 
•	React framework for frontend 
•	XML parsing libraries for RSS processing
